REMARK   1 A dehydrogenated protein fragment plus a free lysine substrate
REMARK   1 that already carries the hydrogens mdprep placed from a manifest
REMARK   1 SMILES.  Those hydrogen names (HAA, HB/HBA, HZ/HZA, HXT) are the
REMARK   1 ones mdprep.ligands.hydrogenate derives from the parent atom, and
REMARK   1 no OpenMM residue template lists them.  Coordinates are LIG A 301
REMARK   1 of 6NIE, the BesD halogenase substrate, which the deposition
REMARK   1 records as LYS A 301.  It is called LIG here because mdprep
REMARK   1 refuses a ligand whose residue name an Amber force field
REMARK   1 already defines: tleap would build it from the protein
REMARK   1 template, and LYS would redirect every lysine in the chain.
